      ```
      makeBrainAideContent({
        name = "obsidian",
        command = "npx",
        args = ["@bitbonsai/mcpvault", "<vault-path>"],
      }: { name?: string; command?: string; args?: string[] })
      ```

      The emitted YAML must contain ONLY `name` and `mcpServerConfig`
      (with `command` and `args` underneath). No `connector`, no
      `rootPath`, no `entryFile`, no `tools`. Body must include the
      `## Prose` heading followed by at least one line of text so the
      parser returns `kind: "ok"`. Default args mirror the canonical
      scaffold from the spec's Good examples (`@bitbonsai/mcpvault`
